- op: discuss  # 3c63
  at: '2026-05-01T19:31:01Z'  # 3c63
  by: agent  # 3c63
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3c63
  clock: 2  # 3c63
  nonce: 3c63  # 3c63
  message: "AUDIT VERDICT: DOCUMENT (with re-eval trigger) — three axes mixed but blast radius is bounded.\n\nFOUR LEAKAGE TESTS — DataModelKind enum (7 values: DATACLASS, DOMAIN_MODEL, DTO, ENTITY, ORM_MODEL, PYDANTIC_MODEL, SCHEMA):\n\n- Test 1 (Property derivability): DATACLASS is derivable from a Python @dataclass decorator on the symbol — already detectable elsewhere. ENTITY is sometimes the JPA @Entity annotation (derivable from decorator), sometimes the DDD architectural concept (NOT derivable from a single property). **PARTIAL LEAKAGE.**\n- Test 2 (Apex/peer): No value plays both 'top type' and 'peer subtype'. **PASSES.**\n- Test 3 (Construct vs relationship): DATACLASS is a language construct (decorator-mechanism); DOMAIN_MODEL is an architectural role; ORM_MODEL/PYDANTIC_MODEL/SCHEMA are library categories; DTO/ENTITY are architectural patterns. **THREE QUESTION-CATEGORIES competing in 7 values. FIRES.**\n- Test 4 (Mechanism vs category): DATACLASS = mechanism (HOW it's expressed in source); ENTITY = category (WHAT architectural role it plays). **FIRES.**\n\nTHE CONFUSION, NAMED: the field tries to answer 'what kind of data model is this?' but the 7 values answer three different versions of that question:\n- HOW it's expressed in source code (construct axis): DATACLASS, NAMEDTUPLE, etc.\n- WHICH library/framework (framework axis): ORM_MODEL, PYDANTIC_MODEL, SCHEMA\n- WHAT architectural role it plays (DDD-pattern axis): DTO, DOMAIN_MODEL, ENTITY\n\nA class can simultaneously be a Python @dataclass (construct), a Pydantic BaseModel (framework — wait, Pydantic models aren't dataclasses, but the example is real for ORM cases), AND a DTO (architectural role). The current single-value enum forces a pick.\n\nVERDICT — DOCUMENT, NOT DEPRECATE-NOW:\n\nThe architectural fix (split into orthogonal data_model_construct + data_model_framework + data_model_role fields) is correct but invasive. Reasons NOT-NOW:\n\n1. Downstream blast radius is bounded. DataModelKind has limited consumer reach today — datamodels.py contains its detection regex table and the DataModel dataclass; no other module hardcodes a set of these values that I found. The drift linter (post WI-variv-lujug) would catch any new such consumer at commit time.\n2. Multi-axis classification needs new detection logic, not just a field-shape change. Detecting DATACLASS independently of ENTITY independently of DTO requires three separate detection passes; the existing regex table assumes one verdict per class.\n3. Property test we already have (registry membership of any *DATA_MODEL_KIND* set) catches the only failure mode that can silently break consumers — a value going stale in a hardcoded set.\n\nDOCUMENT NOW: add a docstring section to DataModelKind clarifying the three-axis confusion explicitly: 'this enum currently mixes construct (DATACLASS), framework (ORM_MODEL, PYDANTIC_MODEL, SCHEMA), and architectural-role (DTO, DOMAIN_MODEL, ENTITY) axes. A symbol may legitimately satisfy all three; the current detection picks one verdict per symbol via the regex table at lines ~94-115. Do not extend without considering whether the new value belongs on a separate axis.'\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS (any one is sufficient):\n1. A consumer needs to filter by the construct OR framework OR role axis independently (e.g., 'all dataclasses' OR 'all Pydantic models, regardless of role'). Today no consumer needs this.\n2. The detection table grows past ~12 values — that's the cardinality where three-axis confusion becomes navigationally hostile.\n3. A single class is observed that should plausibly be tagged with values from two different axes (e.g., a Pydantic BaseModel that is also a DTO — the regex table picks PYDANTIC_MODEL, losing the DTO information silently).\n\nFOLLOW-UP: filing WI-(new) for the docstring update at DataModelKind in datamodels.py."  # 3c63
